-- title:
--   queryCore computes the sum of Lemma 28 from the encodings and the trie of a tile (pruned encodings)
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a program of the light language whose procedure number $53$ is the body of `queryCore`, and in which the routines `nineFirst`, `nineNext`, `scatter`, `horner` and `lookup` meet their specifications for the limits $\mathrm{lim}$. Then `queryCore` meets its specification for $\mathrm{lim}$:
--
--   consider the encodings $\mathrm{enc}_A,\mathrm{enc}_B$ of a tile at $a_A,a_B$ ($10^L$ cells each), a trie array $T$ at $\mathit{tr}$ with the root $\mathit{root}$ of the tile's trie, an output string $\eta$ of $L$ symbols with exactly $m$ inner levels whose digits are stored at $\mathit{wd}$, and scratch areas $\mathit{ss}$ ($m$ cells) and $\mathit{box}$ ($L$ cells). Assume the standing assumptions on the limits, $t\le m$, that every box the query reads is found in the trie, that every partial sum of the query and every product $\mathrm{enc}_A(\tau)\,\mathrm{enc}_B(\tau)$ at a leaf $\tau$ with at most $m$ nines fits in a word, $10^L\le\mathrm{word}$, and that the scratch areas are disjoint from each other and from the data, all within memory. Then for every depth $d$ with $d+1\le\mathrm{depth}$, the call $\mathrm{queryCore}(a_A,a_B,\mathit{tr},\mathit{root},\mathit{wd},\mathit{ss},\mathit{box},L,m,t)$ ends within
--   $$2\,t_{\mathrm{nineFirst}}(m)+\ell\,\big(t_{\mathrm{scatter}}(L)+t_{\mathrm{horner}}(L)+t_{\mathrm{nineNext}}(m)+90\big)+k\,\big(t_{\mathrm{scatter}}(L)+t_{\mathrm{lookup}}(L)+t_{\mathrm{nineNext}}(m)+90\big)+120$$
--   steps, where $\ell$ is the number of leaves of order below $t$ and $k$ the number of boxes that the query reads, and returns
--   $$\sum_{\tau\text{ of order}<t}\mathrm{enc}_A(\tau)\,\mathrm{enc}_B(\tau)\;+\sum_{\text{boxes }\mathbf b\text{ of }\eta}\mathrm{val}_T(\mathbf b),$$
--   the products at the leaves of $\eta$ of order below $t$ plus the values the trie holds for the boxes of $\eta$; only the two scratch areas change. When the trie holds the true box values this is the sum of Lemma 28, i.e. the entry of the product for the query.
--
--   All leaves read have at most $m$ nines, so the routine is correct on pruned encodings.
--
--   “Procedure $p$ meets its specification within $T$ steps” means: called at any depth $d$ allowed by the hypothesis, with the given argument values and a memory $\mu$ satisfying the precondition, the body of $p$ terminates within $T$ steps without violating the limits, and the returned value and final memory satisfy the postcondition.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is `P[Proc.queryCore]? = some queryCoreBody → Light.Sec4.Query.Callees lim P → QueryCoreSpecP lim P`, where `Callees` bundles the specifications of the five routines; the returned value is `trieQuery m t (arrT encA) (arrT encB) T root (digitsO η)`.
